# Applies to the repo-root build context — used only by qa/Dockerfile.test (server/ and client/
# each have their own .dockerignore for their own production image builds).
#
# Without this, `COPY . /workspace` (which runs AFTER `npm ci` has already installed clean,
# correct-platform dependencies) would copy any host node_modules/ on top of them — silently
# replacing a clean install with whatever's on the machine running `docker compose build`,
# wrong-platform native bindings (bcrypt, etc.) included — and could pull real secrets from a
# developer's .env files into the image, and bloat/slow the build context upload.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.docker.example
.git
*.log
